+++ b/README.md
@@ -17,3 +17,67 @@ make demo-data  # load sample rows for local browsing
 ```
 
 The API listens on the port given by `PORT`, default 3000.
+
+## Finding a free slot
+
+`GET /availability` answers "when is this room free?" so a client does not have
+to guess a time, get a 409, and try again.
+
+```bash
+curl 'localhost:3000/availability?from=2030-01-01T09:00:00Z&to=2030-01-01T17:00:00Z&durationMinutes=60&minCapacity=8'
+```
+
+| Query param       | Default         | Meaning                                                 |
+| ----------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `roomId`          | every room      | Restrict to one room; 404 if it does not exist.         |
+| `from`            | now             | Start of the search window.                             |
+| `to`              | `from` + 7 days | End of the search window, at most 31 days after `from`. |
+| `durationMinutes` | 30              | Hide gaps shorter than this.                            |
+| `minCapacity`     | —               | Only rooms that seat at least this many people.         |
+| `limit`/`offset`  | 20 / 0          | Paginate over rooms, as on the other collections.       |
+
+The response pages over rooms and echoes the window that was searched. Rooms
+with nothing free stay in the page with an empty `slots` array, so the totals
+line up with `GET /rooms`.
+
+```json
+{
+  "data": [
+    {
+      "room": { "id": "ckz…", "name": "Aurora", "capacity": 6, "floor": null },
+      "slots": [
+        {
+          "startsAt": "2030-01-01T09:00:00.000Z",
+          "endsAt": "2030-01-01T10:00:00.000Z",
+          "durationMinutes": 60
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "pagination": { "total": 1, "limit": 20, "offset": 0 },
+  "window": { "from": "…", "to": "…", "durationMinutes": 60 }
+}
+```
+
+A booking that still lands on a taken slot comes back with the next openings of
+the length that was asked for, ready to be posted back unchanged:
+
+```json
+{
+  "error": {
+    "code": "BOOKING_CONFLICT",
+    "message": "Room is already booked for this period",
+    "details": {
+      "conflictingBookingId": "ckz…",
+      "suggestions": [{ "startsAt": "…", "endsAt": "…" }]
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Bookings are half-open intervals: one ending exactly when the next starts is not
+a conflict. `endsAt` must be after `startsAt`.
+
+Conflicts are detected by reading before writing, which is not atomic — two
+simultaneous requests for the same slot can still both succeed. Serialising them
+needs a database-level constraint and is not done yet.
